    "https://evergladesuniversity.isolvedhire.com/jobs/1860769": {
      "title": "Academic Scheduler",
      "description": "Academic Scheduler - Boca Raton, FL - Everglades University Jobs Jobs Login Back to all jobs Academic Scheduler Posted 09-Sep-2026 (EST) 5002 T-Rex Avenue #100, Boca Raton, Florida 33431, USA Full Time OOP Email Me Similar Jobs Email Me This Job The Academic Scheduler will be responsible for the publishing of all academic course schedules online and on campus. This position works closely with the Registrar, Academic Advisors, Deans, and Vice President of Academic Affairs staff to ensure course schedules are developed according to student curricular needs. The Academic Scheduler provides oversight, monitoring and configuration of all academic scheduling data for each department and campus. The Academic Scheduler is required to have proficiency with scheduling software, the university's Student Information System, the university's Learning Management System, and with other applications such as Office products, especially Excel. The Academic Scheduler must also have excellent communication and project management and multitask skills to manage and solve complex problems in a fast-paced environment. Responsibilities Develop, build, and maintain the schedule of classes each term, both for online division and ground campus locations. Consult with Deans and Academic Advisors and Registrars regarding courses and classroom scheduling. Manage registration and monitors course/section enrollments and alters/adds/closes sections as needed. Monitor related computer information systems and communicate changes, conflicts, and resolutions to campus academic teams. Resolves specific student enrollment problems during registration period Prepare reports for each campus and updates to the Vice President of Academic Affairs staff on progress with course scheduling, software issues, and process gaps or opportunities for systems improvement. Monitor enrollment and update schedules for newly enrolled or withdrawn students Maintain currency and training with all university information systems such as scheduling software, LMS, SIS, and other associated applications. Monitor enrollment and efficiency of scheduling. Assist with oversight of campus faculty assignments and payroll budgets. Advise the academic and curricular teams of any issues with course sequencing, content, and associated matters. Attend and assist in coordinating or delivering training on academic schedules, curriculum, student issues, best practices and faculty issues related to scheduling and credentialing. Prepare annual reports of schedules year over year and project future projects. Assist with and participate in University-wide events such as graduation and Faculty Convocation. Review and update job description. Special projects and tasks as assigned. Qualifications Earned Bachelor's Degree from an accredited institution required. 1 year of administrative and/or customer service experience. Apply now How would you like to verify your identity? Continue with phone Verify with a one-time text code Continue with email Verify with a one-time code Powered by iSolved Talent Acquisition Sign Up For Job Alerts! Name You must type a name. Email You must type a valid email. Location (city, state or zip code) You must select a location. Accept Terms of Service I agree to the terms of service and privacy policy. You must accept the terms of service and privacy policy. Send Me Jobs Would you like Refer.io to send you similar jobs from other employers? Yes, daily! Yes, weekly! No, thanks. Please type the job title you are interested in: Job title You must type a job title. We'll send some jobs to you in the next 30 minutes. If you don't see them, check your spam folder. Next Resume Input Select file Resume File You must select a file. Upload Resume upload later Thank you for subscribing to receive job alerts. You should start receiving emails in the next week. Your file is uploading. Please wait a few seconds. Enter your phone number if you'd like to receive job alerts for 